e\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Lint clean\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Implementation matches AC\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Solution fits project architecture\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Tests green\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read — positive-path-only evidence is not accepted\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"If review does not accept the work — verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\\\",\\\"done\\\":true}],\\\"notes\\\":\\\"spawn workload selection: class=implementation source=explicit policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=muse/muse-spark/max pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:009eecf230ad676c71fa02f210ad171dc6936cae601b3bc028fa753d219ff3c1 rationale=\\\\\\\"First leaf of STORY-260830-2t4g7i (production tmux backend): dedicated -S server management with owner-only runtime directories, the background-caller credential refusal and a hard determinism constraint. muse-spark max is rank 1 for implementation in the fresh snapshot and is the operator's producer routing for this epic.\\\\\\\"\\\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: muse via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[muse,codex,claude], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\\\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260921-e93883, max_parallel=20)\\\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260921-e93883)\\\\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (muse) (exit=0)\\\\nspawn run completed: muse (run=RUN-260921-e93883, pid=39407, exit=0)\\\\nspawn workload selection: class=review source=explicit policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=claude/claude-opus-5/max pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:dd9abb977b5b89fdf2151c43c20e944d7ed0ca7e20f61d52e87424a10564fe3c rationale=\\\\\\\"Independent review of the first-leaf CR1 of TASK-260830-35urbp; operator routing: independent reviews on claude-opus-5 max (PR48) while producers stay on muse-spark max; codex Astra remains the fallback ceiling.\\\\\\\"\\\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[muse,codex,claude], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\\\\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (claude) (run=RUN-260921-0245e5, max_parallel=20)\\\\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (claude) (run=RUN-260921-0245e5)\\\\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (claude) (exit=0)\\\\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260921-0245e5, pid=70036, exit=0)\\\\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=explicit policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=muse/muse-spark/max pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:009eecf230ad676c71fa02f210ad171dc6936cae601b3bc028fa753d219ff3c1 rationale=\\\\\\\"Rework of CR rev1 of TASK-260830-35urbp: two P1 classes (Windows test compile; a forked attestation gate that admits a wrong generation), four P2 and four P3. Design-level change consuming the landed terminalbackend admission; muse-spark max is rank 1 for implementation in the fresh snapshot and owns the rev1 candidate.\\\\\\\"\\\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: muse via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[muse,codex,claude], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\\\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260921-6e7be5, max_parallel=20)\\\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260921-6e7be5)\\\",\\\"outcomeResources\\\":[{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-35urbp_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--muse-_RUN-260921-e93883.log\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--muse-_RUN-260921-e93883.log\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"System spawn log captured by task-board\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-35urbp_results.md\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_results.md\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Handoff evidence\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-35urbp_conformance-matrix.md\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_conformance-matrix.md\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Clause-to-test matrix\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-35urbp_producer-evidence.tar.gz\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_producer-evidence.tar.gz\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Test and mutant logs tarball\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-35urbp_change-request_rev1.patch\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_change-request_rev1.patch\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Change Request CR-TASK-260830-35urbp-1 revision 1 candidate patch (repository_delta=present, 22 changed paths)\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-35urbp_change-request_rev1-validation.log\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_change-request_rev1-validation.log\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Change Request CR-TASK-260830-35urbp-1 revision 1 bounded validation log\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-35urbp_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--claude-_RUN-260921-0245e5.log\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--claude-_RUN-260921-0245e5.log\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"System spawn log captured by task-board\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-35urbp_review-verdict-rev1.md\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_review-verdict-rev1.md\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Review verdict for CR rev1: CHANGES REQUESTED (P1 windows vet gate broken; P1 forked attestation gate admits wrong-generation/cached evidence; P2 nine surviving narrowings, Windows arm, missing adapter bound, dead inputs; P3 evidence accuracy)\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-35urbp_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Reviewer evidence archive rev1: all 30 configured commands rerun on tree e0d9a81b, tmux-free package run, producer harness x2, reviewer battery x2 with raw per-row logs, 16 probes, coverprofile\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-35urbp_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--muse-_RUN-260921-6e7be5.log\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--muse-_RUN-260921-6e7be5.log\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"System spawn log captured by task-board\\\"}]}\\n===\\nManage attached resources such as screenshots, docs, logs, and other files.\\n\\nUse \\\"task-board resource add\\\" to create a new attached resource, \\\"task-board\\nresource adopt\\\" to register an orphaned local payload, \\\"task-board resource\\nupdate\\\" to replace an existing one, \\\"task-board resource delete\\\" to remove it,\\nand \\\"task-board resource get\\\" to materialize a resource back to the local\\nfilesystem for inspection.\\n\\nUsage:\\n  task-board resource [command]\\n\\nAvailable Commands:\\n  add         Attach a new file resource to an element\\n  adopt       Register an existing unreferenced local resource payload\\n  delete      Delete a resource from an element (requires --confirm)\\n  get         Download a resource to the local filesystem\\n  update      Replace an existing file resource on an element\\n\\nFlags:\\n  -h, --help   help for resource\\n\\nGlobal Flags:\\n      --board-dir string         Path to the board directory (overrides TASK_BOARD_DIR and config local.board_dir) (default \\\".task-board\\\")\\n      --context-profile string   Agent context profile override: full or lite\\n      --insecure                 Skip TLS certificate verification (for self-signed certs)\\n      --json                     Output in JSON format\\n      --no-update-check          Disable automatic update check\\n      --remote string            Remote board server URL (overrides TASK_BOARD_REMOTE)\\n      --remote-board string      Remote board ID (overrides TASK_BOARD_ID)\\n\\nUse \\\"task-board resource [command] --help\\\" for more information about a command.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 9816,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2454,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
