{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c54b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c3b6-e69d-7952-b5c2-99ff4034d208"},"sequence":256,"recorded_at":1780531400000507,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5d75c7b3-ca89-4158-8f1c-936a31a9dfe8","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5d75c7b3-ca89-4158-8f1c-936a31a9dfe8","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5d75c7b3-ca89-4158-8f1c-936a31a9dfe8"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c3b7-b3bd-77c0-ace6-a28a3117adb0"},"task_id":"01a0c3b7-b3bd-77c0-ace6-a28a3117adb0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c3b7-b3bd-77c0-ace6-a28a3117adb0","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/t35/results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-35urbp results — implement-private-tmux-server-management\n2|\n3|First leaf of STORY-260830-2t4g7i (production-tmux-backend, EPIC M1).\n4|Candidate: UNCOMMITTED working tree on branch\n5|`task-board/story/STORY-260830-2t4g7i` atop trunk `799c338`.\n6|No commit, rebase, branch, or merge operation performed by this run.\n7|`git status` shows only `internal/tmuxserver/`, `README.md`, `LOGBOOK.md`.\n8|\n9|Normative source: the pinned `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`\n10|§4.2 tmux backend (lines 1403-1449), with §4.C (1082), §4.D (1220),\n11|and §4.E (1309) as context. All clause citations below name the\n12|pinned file, never the network, never v0.5.0.\n13|\n14|The predecessor leaf TASK-260830-2056mm (pane/terminal-instance\n15|binding, `internal/termbind`) was read before starting, including its\n16|results and conformance matrix: this leaf sits under that binding as\n17|the server-management substrate and reuses its vocabulary (UUIDv7\n18|instance/session identity, closed-shape discipline, no-replace plus\n19|fsync plus hooks plus real-kill crash pattern).\n20|\n21|## Deliverable\n22|\n23|New `internal/tmuxserver`, composing the landed owners (never forked):\n24|\n25|- (1) Runtime custody: `EnsureRuntimeDir` / `VerifyRuntimeDir` create\n26|  and verify the owner-only runtime directory. Containment, mode, and\n27|  ownership are three independent gates, each refusing alone. The\n28|  commit opens the parent through a pinned handle and creates the leaf\n29|  with `mkdirat` (unix), so a symlinked intermediate cannot redirect\n30|  it; mode `0700` is enforced explicitly only on created leaves\n31|  (umask), while pre-existing leaves verify as-is and a widened mode\n32|  refuses instead of being silently repaired.\n33|- (2) Dedicated socket: `SocketPath` / `ResolveSocket` derive the one\n34|  `-S` socket from the runtime directory and refuse any explicit\n35|  override on all four ambient vectors (TMUX environment value,\n36|  inherited socket, default path, conventional name), plus the\n37|  degenerate ambient-collision case.\n38|- (3) Acquisition: `Acquire` attaches or spawns on the foreground\n39|  path and brokers-or-refuses on the background path. The miss path\n40|  returns the typed `capability_unavailable` (exit 6, all five\n41|  Section 15.3 details) and never falls back to direct creation: the\n42|  miss path consults the creation gate by call, and every background\n43|  test arms a spy spawner asserting zero calls.\n44|- (4) Readiness: `CheckLiveAttestation` / `CheckBrokerContact` admit\n45|  only a complete live sentinel-plus-smoke observation bound to the\n46|  exact generation, provider build, and macOS version. The\n47|  `launchctl managername` hint and cached observations travel\n48|  diagnostics-only and authorize nothing (a distinct unconvertible\n49|  type plus behavioral tests).\n50|- (5) Spawn argv: `BuildArgv` emits exactly\n51|  `tmux -S socket new-session -d -s session ax pane session`\n52|  through the landed argv gate.\n53|\n54|Extended vs deliberately not extended:\n55|\n56|- Extended (composed): `axerror.NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable` (typed\n57|  refusal), `axpane` caller vocabulary, `scalar` path/platform/UUIDv7\n58|  grammars, `secprim` Guard lexical join / `OpenNoFollowDir` /\n59|  `CheckArgv` / `IsEnvName`, the `hosttrust` verify-never-repair\n60|  custody precedent, the `termbind`/`axpane` crash-hook pattern.\n61|- Deliberately not extended: `hosttrust` custody itself (Host Channel\n62|  authority with its own lock/binding model — a tmux runtime dir is\n63|  not a trust store, so the leaf owns its lighter commit while\n64|  following the same verify-never-repair rule); `terminstance`\n65|  lifecycle execution (sibling leaf owns operations); `secprim`'s\n66|  private `guardRootMatches` (mirrored as `handleBoundToPath` with a\n67|  seam because the original is unexported); `terminalbackend`\n68|  manifest/probe/evidence admission (cited landed, not re-owned);\n69|  `internal/traceability` (untouched per the producer — bindings and\n70|  the re-pin belong to the final leaf).\n71|\n72|Determinism: every broker, server, and spawner interaction runs\n73|through injected dependencies. No test starts a tmux process, and the\n74|suite passes with no tmux installed. No AC row has a real-tmux\n75|witness — that is the design, not a gap (bound B1). tmux 3.6a being\n76|present on this host was never consulted.\n77|\n78|## Coverage ratio (measured, not planned)\n79|\n80|**54 of 54 AC rows driven** through production entries by named\n81|committed tests — matrix in `internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`,\n82|reproduced with spec-clause mapping in\n83|`TASK-260830-35urbp_conformance-matrix.md`. Row 15's Windows-only\n84|tripwire is compile-verified (`GOOS=windows go build` green) and\n85|executes only on Windows; its unix twin drove the row here.\n86|\n87|## Mutants (shipped harness, per-plant raw logs)\n88|\n89|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py` —\n90|29 narrowing + 1 supplementary additive (D-background-fallback,\n91|labeled) + 1 harmless SURVIVED control. Pass 1 and pass 2: **31/31\n92|each, verdict lists identical**, exit 0. Per-row raw logs (go output +\n93|subprocess exit) for both passes are in the evidence tarball;\n94|production blobs byte-identical before/after every run\n95|(`git status` shows only candidate paths). No token-preserving\n96|source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text (stated\n97|bound B4, harness executes the behavioral suite). The two\n98|nil-dependency narrowings kill by panic (disclosed in the harness\n99|and the matrix): the admitted request calls the nil dependency and\n100|the panic fails the test.\n101|\n102|## Crash / idempotency\n103|\n104|Real SIGKILL seam (unix): `TestEnsureCrashChildSelfTerminates`\n105|(child runs the genuine `EnsureRuntimeDir` entry and kills itself in\n106|`AfterMkdir`, after mkdirat and before verification plus parent\n107|fsync; parent proves the retry converges to the one verified\n108|directory). Idempotent replay: `TestEnsureRuntimeDirIsIdempotent`,\n109|`TestAcquireCreatesRuntimeDirIdempotently`,\n110|`TestAcquireForegroundSpawnIsIdempotentAcrossRetry` (spawn-then-retry\n111|attaches with exactly one spawn).\n112|\n113|## Validation\n114|\n115|`go vet ./...` exit 0, `gofmt -l internal/` empty,\n116|`go test ./... -count=1` 45/45 packages green, 0 FAIL,\n117|`go test ./... -cover -count=1` 45/45 green, 0 FAIL,\n118|`go test ./internal/tmuxserver/ -cover` 87.5% statements\n119|(89 subtests, 0 FAIL), `GOOS=windows go build` green.\n120|Reran myself in this session: everything above, plus the mutant\n121|battery three times total (smoke subset + two full logged passes).\n122|Accepted from already-attached evidence: nothing — this is the\n123|first leaf and no prior evidence exists for it.\n124|\n125|Note on the producer's \"30 configured commands\": the\n126|`task-board.config.json` in this worktree carries no\n127|`validation.commands` section (count 0, verified by read), so there\n128|is no 30-command suite to run here; the AGENTS.md gates above are\n129|what was executed. `task-board validate` (board structure) was also\n130|run green before handoff.\n131|\n132|`internal/traceability` untouched; README gained a package section\n133|with exact test commands and no CLI/capability claim; LOGBOOK gained\n134|one newest-first entry. The candidate is UNCOMMITTED in the Story\n135|worktree.\n136|\n137|## Rejection-pattern self-check\n138|\n139|(a) Literals asserted from spec text at entries (`capability_unavailable`\n140|plus all five typed details, exit 6; `ax`/`pane`/UUID session tail;\n141|`0700`; caller vocabulary), never production constants. (b) Every rule\n142|driven through the entry the matrix names; the creation gate is\n143|enforced by a call on the background miss path so its narrowing kills\n144|through `Acquire`, not only through the helper. (c) Landed owners\n145|composed (listed above) — only package-specific rules are new;\n146|delegated wirings narrow at our call sites with reroute kills. (d)\n147|Inputs driven, effects asserted (spy call counts, argv bytes, socket\n148|equality, typed details); no census stands in for behavior. (e) 29\n149|narrowing rows + labeled additive + applied SURVIVED control, one raw\n150|log per plant per run. (f) Every \"never/composes\" sentence is backed\n151|by a failing-without test (spy assertions, non-use proofs, hint/cache\n152|behavioral rows) or stated as an explicit bound (B1-B8).","final_result":true}}}
