{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c54f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c3b6-e69d-7952-b5c2-99ff4034d208"},"sequence":258,"recorded_at":1780531400000511,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5d75c7b3-ca89-4158-8f1c-936a31a9dfe8","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5d75c7b3-ca89-4158-8f1c-936a31a9dfe8","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5d75c7b3-ca89-4158-8f1c-936a31a9dfe8"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c3b7-b3dc-7701-ae78-119bb3c8f6f9"},"task_id":"01a0c3b7-b3dc-7701-ae78-119bb3c8f6f9","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c3b7-b3dc-7701-ae78-119bb3c8f6f9","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/t35/matrix.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-35urbp conformance matrix — implement-private-tmux-server-management\n2|\n3|Authority: pinned `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`. Every row names the\n4|spec clause in the spec's own words, the production call site, and the\n5|named committed test that drives it through that entry. 54 of 54 rows\n6|driven. Bounds B1-B8 are stated in `internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n7|\n8|## §4.2 dedicated -S server; no ambient/default discovery or reuse\n9|\n10|| # | Clause (spec words) | Call site | Test |\n11||---|---------------------|-----------|------|\n12|| 16 | AX MUST use its dedicated `-S` server | `SocketPath` (socket.go) | TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir |\n13|| 17 | MUST NOT discover or reuse the default server by ambient socket name, under hostile ambient on all five members | `ResolveSocket` (socket.go) | TestResolveSocketDerivesIgnoringAmbient |\n14|| 18 | Ambient facts observed without use | `ObserveAmbient` (socket.go) | TestObserveAmbientRecordsWithoutUsing, TestObserveAmbientNilLookupKeepsOutOfBand |\n15|| 19 | Environment-variable vector refuses with no spawn | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/environment_variable |\n16|| 20 | Inherited-socket vector refuses with no spawn | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/inherited_socket |\n17|| 21 | Default-path vector refuses with no spawn | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/default_path |\n18|| 22 | Conventional-name vector refuses with no spawn | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/conventional_name |\n19|| 23 | Ambient value colliding with the derived socket refuses | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesAmbientCollision, TestResolveSocketRefusesAmbientCollision |\n20|| 40 | Absent server spawns dedicated with exact -S argv disjoint from every ambient vector | `Acquire` via `BuildArgv` | TestAcquireForegroundSpawnsDedicatedServer |\n21|| 41 | Running attested dedicated server attaches with no second spawn | `Acquire` | TestAcquireForegroundAttachesToRunningAttested |\n22|| 46 | Spawn vector carries the dedicated -S socket | `BuildArgv` (argv.go) | TestBuildArgvAddressesOnlyTheDerivedSocket |\n23|| 47 | Ambient sockets refuse at the spawn vector | `BuildArgv` (argv.go) | TestBuildArgvRefusesAmbientSocket (4 subtests) |\n24|\n25|## §4.2 credential-sensitive creation; background broker-or-refuse\n26|\n27|| # | Clause (spec words) | Call site | Test |\n28||---|---------------------|-----------|------|\n29|| 24 | A background CLI MAY contact an already-running authenticated Aqua broker and its attested AX tmux server (macOS, credential-dependent) | `Acquire` via `CheckBrokerContact` | TestAcquireBackgroundContactsBroker |\n30|| 25 | If neither exists it MUST return `capability_unavailable` with typed realm/readiness details: no broker | `Acquire` | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/no_broker |\n31|| 26 | Same: unauthenticated broker | `Acquire` | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/unauthenticated_broker |\n32|| 27 | Same: unattested server | `Acquire` | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/unattested_server |\n33|| 28 | Same: sentinel-only attestation | `Acquire` | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/sentinel-only_attestation |\n34|| 29 | Linux background miss likewise refuses without fallback | `Acquire` | TestAcquireBackgroundMissOnLinuxAlsoRefusesWithoutFallback |\n35|| 30 | Broker probe failure is unknown, never unavailable, with no spawn | `Acquire` | TestAcquireBackgroundProbeFailurePassesThrough |\n36|| 31 | A Background caller MUST NOT create a credential-dependent tmux server; MUST NOT fall back to direct server creation | `checkCreationAllowed` via `Acquire` | TestCheckCreationAllowedRefusesBackground, TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable (N-creation-literal kill path) |\n37|| 42 | Running unattested server refuses with no spawn and no repair | `Acquire` | TestAcquireForegroundRefusesRunningUnattested |\n38|| 43 | Server probe failure is unknown, never absent, with no spawn | `Acquire` | TestAcquireForegroundProbeFailurePassesThrough |\n39|| 44 | Spawn failure reports with exactly one attempt and no fallback | `Acquire` | TestAcquireForegroundSpawnFailureReportsWithoutFallback |\n40|| 45 | Malformed session refuses before any spawn | `Acquire` via `BuildArgv` | TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession |\n41|| 48 | Session identity follows the landed UUIDv7 wiring | `BuildArgv` (argv.go) | TestBuildArgvRefusesMalformedSession |\n42|| 54 | Spawn-then-retry converges to the one server with exactly one spawn | `Acquire` | TestAcquireForegroundSpawnIsIdempotentAcrossRetry |\n43|\n44|## §4.2 managername hint only; cached observations never authorize\n45|\n46|| # | Clause (spec words) | Call site | Test |\n47||---|---------------------|-----------|------|\n48|| 32 | `launchctl managername` is a diagnostic hint only; a cached sentinel or prior `managername` observation MUST NOT authorize resume (background) | `Acquire` | TestAcquireBackgroundHintAndCacheAuthorizeNothing |\n49|| 33 | Same (foreground: cached pass fakes no running server) | `Acquire` | TestAcquireForegroundHintAndCacheChangeNothing |\n50|| 34 | Functional AX sentinel inside the exact server plus separate provider-auth smoke admits | `CheckLiveAttestation` (readiness.go) | TestCheckLiveAttestationAdmitsComplete |\n51|| 35 | Sentinel-only evidence is insufficient | `CheckLiveAttestation` (readiness.go) | TestCheckLiveAttestationRefusesEachMissingConjunct/sentinel_only_is_insufficient |\n52|| 36 | Smoke-only evidence is insufficient | `CheckLiveAttestation` (readiness.go) | TestCheckLiveAttestationRefusesEachMissingConjunct/smoke_only_is_insufficient |\n53|| 37 | Evidence MUST bind the exact generation, provider build, and macOS version | `CheckLiveAttestation` (readiness.go) | TestCheckLiveAttestationRefusesEachMissingConjunct (3 binding subtests) |\n54|| 38 | Authenticated broker plus attested server admits | `CheckBrokerContact` (readiness.go) | TestCheckBrokerContactAdmitsAuthenticatedAttested |\n55|| 39 | Each missing broker/attestation/smoke fact refuses | `CheckBrokerContact` (readiness.go) | TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact (4 subtests) |\n56|\n57|## §4.C wrapper entrypoint shape (cited)\n58|\n59|| # | Clause (spec words) | Call site | Test |\n60||---|---------------------|-----------|------|\n61|| 46 | Every managed pane MUST run `ax pane <logical-session-id>` (spawn tail) | `BuildArgv` (argv.go) | TestBuildArgvAddressesOnlyTheDerivedSocket, TestAcquireForegroundSpawnsDedicatedServer (tail assertion) |\n62|\n63|## §4.D capability binding (cited landed)\n64|\n65|| # | Clause (spec words) | Call site | Test |\n66||---|---------------------|-----------|------|\n67|| 25-28 | Typed refusal names `credential_capable_execution_realm` with the exact Section 15.3 detail set | `Acquire` via `axerror.NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable` | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable (detail assertions in every subtest) |\n68|\n69|## §4.E owner-only sensitive runtime state\n70|\n71|| # | Clause (spec words) | Call site | Test |\n72||---|---------------------|-----------|------|\n73|| 1 | Runtime directory created owner-only (0700) | `EnsureRuntimeDir` | TestEnsureRuntimeDirCreatesOwnerOnly |\n74|| 2 | Re-ensure converges idempotently | `EnsureRuntimeDir` | TestEnsureRuntimeDirIsIdempotent |\n75|| 3 | Compliant directory verifies | `VerifyRuntimeDir` | TestVerifyRuntimeDirAdmitsCompliant |\n76|| 4 | Widened mode refuses, never silently repaired | `EnsureRuntimeDir`, `VerifyRuntimeDir` | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesWidenedMode |\n77|| 5 | Non-directory leaf refuses | `EnsureRuntimeDir` | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf |\n78|| 6 | Symlink leaf refuses | `EnsureRuntimeDir` | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesSymlinkLeaf |\n79|| 7 | Foreign ownership refuses | `EnsureRuntimeDir`, `VerifyRuntimeDir` | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesForeignOwnership |\n80|| 8 | Handle/path mismatch refuses | `EnsureRuntimeDir` | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesHandleMismatch |\n81|| 9 | Symlinked root refuses | `EnsureRuntimeDir` | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesSymlinkRoot |\n82|| 10 | Malformed and missing roots refuse | `EnsureRuntimeDir` | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesBadRoots (4 subtests) |\n83|| 11 | Malformed names refuse | `EnsureRuntimeDir` | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesBadNames (6 subtests) |\n84|| 12 | Unknown platform refuses | `EnsureRuntimeDir` | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesBadPlatform |\n85|| 13 | Verify refuses absence without creating | `VerifyRuntimeDir` | TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesAbsence |\n86|| 14 | Linux and WSL2 share the unix custody discipline | `EnsureRuntimeDir` | TestLinuxAndWSL2ShareUnixCustody |\n87|| 15 | Windows-on-unix refuses; Windows custody subset pinned | `EnsureRuntimeDir` | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesWindowsOnUnixHost, TestWindowsCustodyBoundIsStated (windows-only) |\n88|| 52 | Acquisition ensures the directory idempotently | `Acquire` via `EnsureRuntimeDir` | TestAcquireCreatesRuntimeDirIdempotently |\n89|| 53 | Crash between mkdir and fsync retries to the one verified directory (real SIGKILL) | `EnsureRuntimeDir` | TestEnsureCrashChildSelfTerminates |\n90|\n91|## §15.3 typed refusal shape (input validation)\n92|\n93|| # | Clause (spec words) | Call site | Test |\n94||---|---------------------|-----------|------|\n95|| 49 | Unknown caller refuses | `Acquire` | TestAcquireRefusesUnknownCaller |\n96|| 50 | Missing typed-detail members refuse instead of emitting untyped | `Acquire` | TestAcquireRefusesMissingRealmDetails (3 subtests) |\n97|| 51 | Missing dependencies refuse on every nil shape | `Acquire` | TestAcquireRefusesMissingDependencies, TestAcquireBackgroundNilBrokerWithSpawnRefuses, TestAcquireForegroundNilSpawnWithProbeRefuses |\n98|\n99|## Mutant-to-gate map (all kills through the production entries above)\n100|\n101|N-mode-create (row 4, create arm), N-mode-verify (row 4, verify arm),\n102|N-ownership-uid (row 7), N-containment-slash (row 11), N-containment-mismatch\n103|(row 8), N-containment-symlink (row 6), N-root-wiring (row 10), N-platform-wiring\n104|(row 12), N-override-env/inherited/default/conventional (rows 19-22),\n105|N-collision (row 23), N-attestation-smoke/sentinel (rows 35-36),\n106|N-attestation-binding (row 37), N-broker-auth/attested (rows 26-27, 39),\n107|N-creation-literal (row 31), N-caller-vocabulary (row 49),\n108|N-details-remediation (row 50), N-unattested-foreground (row 42),\n109|N-spawn-swallow (row 44), N-probe-swallow-foreground/background (rows 43, 30),\n110|N-argv-socket (row 47), N-argv-session (rows 45, 48), N-deps-background/foreground\n111|(row 51), D-background-fallback supplementary (rows 25-28), C-control SURVIVED.","final_result":true}}}
