{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c553","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c3b6-e69d-7952-b5c2-99ff4034d208"},"sequence":260,"recorded_at":1780531400000515,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5d75c7b3-ca89-4158-8f1c-936a31a9dfe8","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5d75c7b3-ca89-4158-8f1c-936a31a9dfe8","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5d75c7b3-ca89-4158-8f1c-936a31a9dfe8"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c3b7-b392-7d61-9f2f-f248ca4e6407"},"task_id":"01a0c3b7-b392-7d61-9f2f-f248ca4e6407","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c3b7-b392-7d61-9f2f-f248ca4e6407","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/t35/verdict.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-35urbp — review verdict, Change Request revision 1\n2|\n3|**Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED** (routed `to-dev`). Two P1 classes, four P2, four P3.\n4|\n5|- Reviewer run: RUN-260921-0245e5 (claude-opus-5 max), reviewing CR-TASK-260830-35urbp-1 rev 1\n6|  published by RUN-260921-e93883 (muse-spark max).\n7|- Reviewed bytes: base `799c338e401fca0b24859c0b870cd665927209f2` (= `origin/main` at review\n8|  time, no trunk drift), candidate tree `e0d9a81b236c9add75805d94df3bc31dbc256562`, patch\n9|  sha256 `650ea3b60b58d799255882a38daffa5118f3e6839b3f715207c0941e35716ba2` (recomputed from the\n10|  tree pair, equal). The live Story worktree's uncommitted tree was recomputed through a\n11|  temporary index and equals the CR tree. Every measurement below was taken on detached,\n12|  immutable copies of that tree (`candidate`, `mutant-copy`, `probe-copy`, all cut from a\n13|  dangling review commit of the CR tree); the live worktree, its index, branch and HEAD were\n14|  not touched, no product edit, commit, checkpoint or integration was performed.\n15|- Normative authority: pinned `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` §4.2 (1403-1449) with §4.C,\n16|  §4.D, §4.E; the task record's v0.5.0 Scope is stale. The candidate cites the pinned file\n17|  only (checked: no v0.5.0 line number, every quoted sentence is present in the pinned file).\n18|\n19|## What was reproduced (all on tree e0d9a81b, PATH without any tmux binary, TMUX/TMUX_TMPDIR unset, no tmux process on the host)\n20|\n21|| Check | Result | Log |\n22|| --- | --- | --- |\n23|| Configured suite, 30 commands (`spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands`) | 30/30 green, every command rerun by this reviewer (1-3, 26-28, 30: `static-gates.log`; 4: `cmd04-06-test-cover.log` + `cmd04-test-v.full.log`, 45 pkgs, 2847 PASS / 0 FAIL / 2 pre-existing SKIP outside this package; 5 race: `cmd05-race.log`, 45 ok, 6m56s; 6 cover: 45 ok; 7-25: `cmd07-25-fuzz-tracecheck-catalog.log`; 29: `cmd29-task-board-validate.log`, exit 0 with the board's pre-existing 180 issues) | `logs/` |\n24|| Package suite, tmux unresolvable | `go test ./internal/tmuxserver -count=1 -v`: 51 top-level tests, 89 PASS lines, 0 FAIL, **0 SKIP**. The determinism claim holds: no row's witness skips without tmux | `pkg-tests-notmux-v.log` |\n25|| Package coverage | 87.5% (matches the results); uncovered production blocks listed in the findings | `tmuxserver-cover.out` |\n26|| Producer harness, two passes | 31/31 both passes (30 KILLED exit 1, C-control SURVIVED exit 0), verdict lists identical, tree clean after each pass, zero `__pycache__`/`.pyc` | `harness-pass1/`, `harness-pass2/` (one raw log per row per pass) |\n27|| Reviewer battery, 14 rows × 2 passes | identical verdicts both passes; see §M | `reviewer-battery-pass1/`, `reviewer-battery-pass2/` |\n28|| Reviewer probes, 16 tests | all behave as predicted; see §P | `probes-rev1.log`, `probe-copy/.../zz_review_probe_test.go` (in the evidence archive) |\n29|| **Hosted CI gate `GOOS=windows go vet ./...`** | **FAILS** — see P1-A | `static-gates.log`, `windows-test-compile.log` |\n30|| Trunk drift / boundary / hygiene | `git diff --name-only 799c338 origin/main` is empty; `internal/traceability` untouched; no `__pycache__`/`.pyc` in the CR tree or any copy; gofmt/vet clean; `GOOS=linux`/`GOOS=windows go build` green | `static-gates.log` |\n31|\n32|## P1 — must fix\n33|\n34|### P1-A. The candidate breaks the repository's hosted CI: the Windows test binary does not compile\n35|\n36|`GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...` (and `go test -c`) fail on the candidate:\n37|\n38|```\n39|internal/tmuxserver/runtime_test.go:103:14: undefined: effectiveUID\n40|internal/tmuxserver/runtime_test.go:104:2: undefined: effectiveUID\n41|internal/tmuxserver/runtime_test.go:105:17: undefined: effectiveUID\n42|```\n43|\n44|`runtime_test.go` carries no build constraint but reassigns the `effectiveUID` seam that only\n45|`ownership_unix.go` (`//go:build !windows`) declares. `.github/workflows/ci.yml:85` (\"Vet\n46|Windows build-tagged sources\", Linters job) and `ci.yml:354` (\"Vet Windows build (includes\n47|test files)\", Windows compile-only job) both run exactly `GOOS=windows go vet ./...`; the\n48|README's CI table (README.md:805) documents that gate as \"test files included\". Trunk is\n49|clean under it; the candidate is the only failing package. The local 30-command suite runs\n50|`GOOS=windows go build` (which compiles no test files), which is why the CR construction\n51|stayed green — the DoD line \"build/validation commands run after changes and build not\n52|broken\" is not met against the repository's documented gate set.\n53|\n54|The results' claim \"Row 15's Windows-only tripwire is compile-verified (`GOOS=windows go\n55|build` green) and executes only on Windows\" is false in both halves: `go build` never\n56|compiles `windows_bound_test.go`, and the package's test binary cannot be built for Windows\n57|at all, so `TestWindowsCustodyBoundIsStated` can never execute. Row 15 is unmeasured.\n58|\n59|Fix: constrain the seam-using tests (`//go:build !windows`, or move the `effectiveUID`\n60|reassignment into a unix-only test file) and prove it with `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` in the\n61|results. See also P2-B for what the Windows arm should be.\n62|\n63|### P1-B. The attestation/readiness model forks a landed gate with a weaker copy, and the weaker copy admits what the spec forbids\n64|\n65|`readiness.go` re-models the §4.2 credential-realm decision as five loose fields\n66|(`LiveAttestation{SentinelPassed, SmokePassed, ServerGeneration, ProviderBuild, MacOSVersion}`,\n67|readiness.go:30-36) decided by `CheckLiveAttestation` (readiness.go:46-57) and a\n68|`BrokerStatus{Authenticated, Attested, Attestation}` (readiness.go:64-68). The repository\n69|already owns exactly this decision:\n70|\n71|- `internal/terminalbackend.Reconcile` / `Registry.AdmitProbe` (manifest.go:1683, :2059) admit\n72|  the `credential_capable_execution_realm` Capability Evidence row with signature\n73|  verification, liveness (`checkEvidenceLiveness`, manifest.go:1923), generation binding\n74|  (`checkProbeGeneration`, manifest.go:1771, `CodeStaleGeneration`), `os_version`,\n75|  `provider_build`, `sentinel_result`, `provider_auth_smoke_result` — the §4.D object whose\n76|  members are the §4.2 sentence \"Evidence MUST bind the exact tmux server generation,\n77|  provider build, and macOS version\" (SPEC 1428-1429; §4.D 1300: \"wrong-generation evidence\n78|  disables the claim\").\n79|- `internal/axpane.checkRealm` (decide.go:913-928) applies it to the §4.2 background-caller\n80|  rule: `admitted.Has(credential_capable_execution_realm)`, `Realm.ServerGeneration ==\n81|  Backend.RawGeneration` (stale generation refuses), host-binding/provider-build cross-bind,\n82|  and the same `axerror.NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable` composition the candidate re-declares in\n83|  `backgroundUnavailable` (acquire.go:237-252). Its `Realm` type documents the landed design\n84|  decision the candidate reverses (decide.go:97-118): \"There is deliberately no member for a\n85|  cached sentinel result, a managername observation, or any attested-server boolean: none\n86|  authorizes resume, so none is an input ... the bare boolean previously carried here never\n87|  authorizes and is removed.\" `internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md:96-97` already claims the\n88|  §4.2 rows \"Background caller without attested server\" and \"Cached evidence never\n89|  authorizes\" against the landed reconcile path.\n90|- The predecessor this leaf was told to sit under, `internal/termbind.ResolveEvidence`\n91|  (resolve.go:77), returns a `terminalbackend.Admitted` — the type this leaf should have\n92|  consumed as its \"attested\" fact.\n93|\n94|The candidate reuses two string constants from axpane and forks the gate. The fork is weaker\n95|in the one dimension this leaf's own rows claim: the \"binding\" arm (readiness.go:53) checks\n96|that three strings are non-empty, never that they bind to anything. Reproduced through the\n97|production entry `Acquire` on both paths (`probes-rev1.log`):\n98|\n99|- `TestReviewHoleForegroundAttachAdmitsWrongGeneration`: request generation `generation-7`,\n100|  probe reports a running server attested for `generation-6` / yesterday's build / yesterday's\n101|  macOS → `attached-running`, admitted.\n102|- `TestReviewHoleBackgroundBrokerAdmitsWrongGeneration`: same on the broker path → `broker`,\n103|  admitted (§4.4 SPEC 1485 also requires broker readiness to be same-user and\n104|  generation-bound; `BrokerStatus` carries neither fact).\n105|- `TestReviewHoleCachedObservationReplayedAsLiveAuthorizes`: a `CachedObservation` copied\n106|  field-by-field into `LiveAttestation` authorizes attach. The \"distinct unconvertible type\"\n107|  (readiness.go:14-19, doc.go, README) is a struct literal away from conversion; nothing in\n108|  the package can tell a cached observation from a live one, which is precisely what\n109|  reconcile's liveness + generation digest exist for (SPEC 1445-1449).\n110|\n111|Consequences for the evidence table: rows 24, 34, 38 drive the fork's predicate, not the\n112|spec's; row 37 (\"Generation-, build-, and macOS-unbound observations refuse\") is driven only\n113|for empty strings — a wrong generation is admitted, so the row is not driven as stated; rows\n114|32-33 (hint and cache \"authorize nothing\") are vacuous: `Request.Hint` and `Request.Cached`\n115|(acquire.go:101-105) are never read by any production statement (grep: zero reads outside\n116|the struct), so the tests prove non-use of two fields the package itself added and nothing\n117|about the spec's cached-sentinel rule, which lives on the reconcile/generation path. README\n118|(\"bound to the exact server generation\"), doc.go (\"the live-attestation authorization gate\n119|over which cached sentinel and managername observations carry no authority\") and\n120|TRACEABILITY rows 34-39 are prose that outruns the tests (rejection pattern f).\n121|\n122|Fix (design, not a patch): drop `LiveAttestation`/`CachedObservation`/`ManagerNameHint`/\n123|`BrokerStatus.Attested` and take the landed admission as input — a\n124|`terminalbackend.Admitted` (or the `termbind.ResolvedEvidence` that carries it) plus the raw\n125|generation, deciding \"attested\" as `Admitted.Has(\"credential_capable_execution_realm\")`\n126|composed with the generation equality axpane already enforces, or call into axpane's realm\n127|predicate if it is exported for this purpose. The broker \"authenticated\" fact is new and may\n128|stay, but it must be typed and generation-bound per §4.4, not a bare boolean. Re-derive rows\n129|24-39 from the composed gate and state as a BOUND whatever the leaf still cannot prove\n130|without a live broker.\n131|\n132|## P2 — must fix or state as a bound\n133|\n134|### P2-A. Nine narrowing mutants survive the committed suite on gates the matrix counts closed\n135|\n136|Reviewer battery (`reviewer-battery-pass{1,2}/verdicts.log`, raw per-row logs with exits).\n137|Each row was run twice per pass: against the committed suite as shipped (full package, no\n138|`-run` mask) and again with the reviewer's probe file added, so every SURVIVED below is\n139|proven to be a real narrowing that one test kills — not an unmeasurable arm.\n140|\n141|| Row | Gate narrowed (site) | Committed suite | With probe | Matrix row it exposes |\n142|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n143|| R-acquire-swallow-commit-refusal | `Acquire` admits every commit-phase custody refusal (`err != nil && dir == \"\"`, acquire.go:137) | SURVIVED | KILLED | 4-9 are pinned at `EnsureRuntimeDir` only; `acquire.go:137-139` is uncovered — no Acquire test stages any runtime-dir refusal |\n144|| R-verify-symlink-fallback | verify side follows a symlink leaf (runtime_unix.go:107) | SURVIVED | KILLED | row 6 covers the commit side only; the producer's N-containment-symlink mutates commit only |\n145|| R-override-tmpdir | override gate admits the `TMUX_TMPDIR` value (socket.go:86) | SURVIVED | KILLED | rows 19-22 pin four literal values of one `override != \"\"` gate; the fifth member — the one tmux uses to relocate its default socket directory — is unpinned |\n146|| R-collision-inherited / -tmuxenv / -tmpdir / -conventional | collision gate admits one member each (socket.go:108) | SURVIVED ×4 | KILLED ×4 | row 23 is pinned on `DefaultPath` only (N-collision) |\n147|| R-argv-env-value | argv gate admits the TMUX environment value (argv.go:17) | SURVIVED | KILLED | row 47 \"4 subtests\" pins four of five members; reach is direct `BuildArgv` only |\n148|| R-fchmod-arm-unmeasured | post-mkdirat `Fchmod` skipped for non-root (runtime_unix.go:55) | SURVIVED | KILLED | row 1's \"enforced explicitly because mkdir honors umask\" is unobserved: the suite runs under umask 022, where mkdirat alone yields 0700 |\n149|\n150|Three additive fallback plants on the background miss path (re-enter foreground creation and\n151|return `spawned`; create when `!NeedsCredentials`; create when `Platform != macos`) were all\n152|KILLED by the committed spies — the no-fallback rule is genuinely pinned along the caller,\n153|credential and platform axes. One delete-only row, R-ambient-vocabulary-dead-arm, SURVIVED\n154|both runs: `ObserveAmbient`'s \"ambient vocabulary\" refusal (socket.go:52-54, uncovered) guards\n155|two package constants that are valid env names and is unreachable; row 18's sentence\n156|\"Unknown variable names refuse rather than being silently skipped\" describes no behaviour.\n157|\n158|### P2-B. The Windows arm implements a tmux runtime directory where the spec forbids claiming tmux, with weaker gates\n159|\n160|§4.3 (SPEC 1458): \"Native Windows MUST NOT claim tmux or tmux resurrection.\" The unix commit\n161|refuses `PlatformWindows` on a unix host, but `runtime_windows.go:23-42` creates an\n162|`ax-tmux` runtime directory on a Windows host with `os.MkdirAll` (builds parents — the\n163|unix arm's comment says the entry \"never builds parents\"), no mode gate, no ownership gate,\n164|and a stated \"custody subset\" bound (B2) where the right behaviour is a typed refusal of\n165|`PlatformWindows` on every host. `_ = filepath.Clean` (runtime_windows.go:40) is an\n166|import-keeping hack. Combined with P1-A the whole Windows story of this leaf is untested and\n167|unrunnable. Fix: refuse `PlatformWindows` in `lexicalRuntimePath` (or the platform gate) with\n168|`tmux_invalid_arguments`, delete the Windows commit/verify arms and the tripwire, and keep the\n169|package compiling and vetting for `GOOS=windows`.\n170|\n171|### P2-C. The AC's \"create dedicated tmux -S servers\" has no production execution path, and the socket write has no crash evidence — neither is stated as a bound\n172|\n173|`Dependencies` (acquire.go:59-66) has no production implementation anywhere in the tree; the\n174|comment \"Production wires live tmux and broker probes; tests wire fakes\" (acquire.go:57)\n175|describes code that does not exist. `BuildArgv` + `Acquire` decide; nothing execs. The brief\n176|named the server socket a durable write requiring crash/idempotency evidence or an explicit\n177|purity bound; B1 states determinism, not the missing adapter. This is a defensible split\n178|with the lifecycle leaf, but it must be written down: state as a BOUND that this leaf ships\n179|the decision core and argv only, that the exec/probe adapters and the socket's crash\n180|evidence are owned by TASK-260830-1c28dz, and remove the \"production wires\" sentence.\n181|\n182|### P2-D. Dead inputs, dead arms and a doc comment that contradicts the code\n183|\n184|- `Request.NeedsCredentials` (acquire.go:90) is never read; `Hint` and `Cached` (see P1-B)\n185|  are never read. Three request members whose only purpose is to be proven unused are API\n186|  surface, not evidence.\n187|- `acquireForeground`'s `checkCreationAllowed` call (acquire.go:201-203, uncovered) can never\n188|  refuse — the caller was already classified foreground.\n189|- `VerifyRuntimeDir` has zero production callers; its doc (runtime.go:50-54) says \"Acquisition\n190|  calls this instead of Ensure: ... a missing directory refuses rather than being silently\n191|  created on the authorizing path\", while `Acquire` (acquire.go:136) calls `EnsureRuntimeDir`\n192|  on every path — including the background path, so a background caller performs the durable\n193|  directory write. Its refusal arms for platform-host, root-open, handle-mismatch and lexical\n194|  failures (runtime_unix.go:96-106, runtime.go:56-58) are all uncovered. Either wire Verify\n195|  into the authorizing path as the comment promises, or delete the comment and the entry.\n196|\n197|## P3 — fix in the same rework\n198|\n199|- P3-A. The results state \"the `task-board.config.json` in this worktree carries no\n200|  `validation.commands` section (count 0, verified by read), so there is no 30-command suite\n201|  to run here\". The 30 commands are at `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands`; the\n202|  producer did not run the configured suite; the CR construction did (attached log footer\n203|  `required=30 green=30`), and this review reran all 30. Report what was read accurately.\n204|- P3-B. Crash convergence is umask-conditional and unstated: a leaf left between `Mkdirat`\n205|  and `Fchmod` under an owner-bit-stripping umask (probe\n206|  `TestReviewObserveCrashRetryUnderRestrictiveUmaskNeverConverges`: mode 0600) refuses\n207|  `runtime mode` on every retry and never converges, because existing leaves are verified,\n208|  never repaired. State the bound (umask ⊆ 0077) or narrow the repair to\n209|  owner-only-and-narrower-than-0700 leaves owned by the caller.\n210|- P3-C. A symlinked intermediate component inside the root path is followed\n211|  (`TestReviewObserveSymlinkedIntermediateInRootIsFollowed`); only the root's last component\n212|  is refused (row 9). This matches secprim's own root open and is acceptable if stated as the\n213|  same bound; today TRACEABILITY says nothing.\n214|- P3-D. `BuildArgv`'s `secprim.CheckArgv` refusal (argv.go:32-34) is uncovered and, on this\n215|  filesystem, reachable only by a direct call with an invalid-UTF-8 runtime dir (APFS refuses\n216|  such names, so not through `Acquire`); state it or drop the arm.\n217|\n218|## Coverage ratio measured against the 54-row table\n219|\n220|51 of 54 rows are driven as stated; rows 15 (Windows tripwire cannot compile, P1-A), 18\n221|(refusal half unreachable) and 37 (measures emptiness, not binding) are not. Of the 51, rows\n222|24, 32, 33, 34 and 38 drive the forked boolean predicate rejected in P1-B rather than the spec\n223|clause they cite. Nine gates counted closed are pinned on one member or one side only (P2-A).\n224|The producer's \"54 of 54\" is therefore inflated by three and rests on a fork for five more.\n225|\n226|## Determinism, forks, boundary — what held\n227|\n228|- Determinism held: 0 SKIP with tmux unresolvable; every witness is deterministic; no\n229|  real-tmux witness exists (B1, honest).\n230|- Custody gates held under attack: FIFO leaf and FIFO root refuse without blocking\n231|  (`O_DIRECTORY` refuses at lookup); symlink leaf refuses on both entries; widened mode,\n232|  foreign UID and handle mismatch refuse; the real-SIGKILL crash test is genuine (child runs\n233|  the production entry and kills itself in `AfterMkdir`).\n234|- The no-fallback rule held against three fallback shapes beyond the producer's D row.\n235|- Path grammar, argv shape, UUIDv7 session and the `capability_unavailable` typed refusal are\n236|  composed from scalar/secprim/axerror, not forked; `internal/traceability` untouched;\n237|  README section carries no CLI/capability claim; LOGBOOK entry is newest-first.\n238|\n239|## Rework scope (for the producer)\n240|\n241|1. Make the package compile and vet for `GOOS=windows` including test files\n242|   (`GOOS=windows go vet ./...` green) and refuse `PlatformWindows` on every host per §4.3;\n243|   delete the Windows commit/verify arms and the tripwire (P1-A, P2-B).\n244|2. Replace `LiveAttestation`/`BrokerStatus.Attested`/`CachedObservation`/`ManagerNameHint`\n245|   with the landed admission (`terminalbackend.Admitted` from\n246|   `Reconcile`/`termbind.ResolveEvidence` + raw generation equality as in\n247|   `axpane.checkRealm`); remove the `Hint`/`Cached`/`NeedsCredentials` request members;\n248|   rewrite rows 24-39 against the composed gate, with a wrong-generation negative and a\n249|   replayed-cached-evidence negative driven through `Acquire`; fix README/doc.go/TRACEABILITY\n250|   prose to match (P1-B, P2-D).\n251|3. Add committed killers for the nine surviving narrowings (an `Acquire` test that stages a\n252|   commit-phase custody refusal; a verify-side symlink leaf; `TMUX_TMPDIR` as override; a\n253|   collision on each of the five members through `Acquire`; the fifth member at the argv gate;\n254|   a umask-0177 create) and ship the corresponding rows in `mutant_harness.py` (P2-A).\n255|4. State the bounds: decision-core-only delivery with the exec/probe adapters and socket\n256|   crash evidence owned by the lifecycle leaf; umask-conditional crash convergence;\n257|   symlinked-intermediate root; the `CheckArgv` arm (P2-C, P3-B..D). Delete or reach the\n258|   dead arms (P2-D).\n259|5. Correct the results: the configured suite exists (30 commands) and must be reported as run;\n260|   report the measured ratio with the three undriven rows named (P3-A).","final_result":true}}}
