{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c999","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c3b6-e69d-7952-b5c2-99ff4034d208"},"sequence":807,"recorded_at":1780531400001609,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5d75c7b3-ca89-4158-8f1c-936a31a9dfe8","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5d75c7b3-ca89-4158-8f1c-936a31a9dfe8","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5d75c7b3-ca89-4158-8f1c-936a31a9dfe8"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c3bb-0f41-78e2-8ec5-eb2c271007e7"},"task_id":"01a0c3bb-0f41-78e2-8ec5-eb2c271007e7","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c3bb-0f41-78e2-8ec5-eb2c271007e7","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-16-1\",\n  \"command\": \"python3 -c \\\"\\nimport json\\ncfg=json.load(open('task-board.config.json'))\\ncmds=cfg['spawn']['worktree_isolation']['validation']['commands']\\nprint('count:',len(cmds))\\nfor i,c in enumerate(cmds,1):\\n    print(i, c.get('name','?'), '|', str(c.get('run',c))[:120])\\n\\\" 2>&1 | head -n 50\\necho \\\"=====README tmuxserver section=====\\\"\\ngrep -n \\\"tmuxserver\\\" README.md | head\\necho \\\"=====LOGBOOK head=====\\\"\\nhead -n 40 LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Read validation commands and docs state\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"Traceback (most recent call last):\\n  File \\\"<string>\\\", line 7, in <module>\\n    print(i, c.get('name','?'), '|', str(c.get('run',c))[:120])\\n             ^^^^^\\nAttributeError: 'str' object has no attribute 'get'\\ncount: 30\\n=====README tmuxserver section=====\\n2329:## Private tmux server management (`tmuxserver` leaf)\\n2331:[`internal/tmuxserver`](internal/tmuxserver) creates owner-only runtime\\n2361:go test ./internal/tmuxserver -count=1\\n2362:go test ./internal/tmuxserver -cover -count=1\\n2369:PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py\\n2380:[the task evidence map](internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md).\\n=====LOGBOOK head=====\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-21\\n\\n### TASK-260830-35urbp — Private tmux server management (first leaf, STORY-260830-2t4g7i)\\n\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/tmuxserver` — the §4.2/§4.C-4.E first leaf over the landed owners: `EnsureRuntimeDir` commits the runtime leaf via `mkdirat` from a pinned root handle with three independent custody gates (containment, exact `0700`, eUID ownership, each refusing alone; existing dirs verified, never repaired); `ResolveSocket` derives the one `-S` socket from the runtime dir and refuses any override on all four ambient vectors (TMUX env, inherited socket, default path, conventional name); `Acquire` attaches/spawns on foreground and brokers-or-refuses on background with the typed `capability_unavailable` (via `axerror.NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable`) and no fallback — the miss path consults the creation gate by call, and every background test arms a zero-call spy spawner; `CheckLiveAttestation` admits only complete live sentinel+smoke bound to generation/build/macOS, while the managername hint and cached observations travel diagnostics-only and authorize nothing; `BuildArgv` emits the exact `tmux -S socket new-session -d -s session ax pane session` vector through the landed argv gate. No test starts tmux: all probes/spawns are injected fakes.\\n- F1: a structural absence (\\\"this path has no spawn call\\\") is not an enforceable gate until a call exists to weaken — the background miss path now consults `checkCreationAllowed` by call so the N-creation-literal narrowing (background admitted) reddens through the entry with the creation code instead of the typed unavailable, and the D-background-fallback additive plant (reviewer-shaped direct-creation call) reddens on the spy assertions.\\n- F2: `Fchmod` before verification silently repairs — the create path now chmods only leaves it created (`Mkdirat` success, for umask) while pre-existing leaves verify as-is, so a widened `0755` refuses on both ensure and verify instead of being narrowed back.\\n- F3: single-member refusal classes still narrow honestly — `caller == \\\"background\\\"` weakens to the capitalized twin (gate present, one member admitted), and delegated wirings (scalar UUIDv7/platform/path grammars) narrow at our call site with reroute kills, never by re-testing the owner.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 29 narrowing mutants plus one supplementary additive row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 31/31 with the harmless SURVIVED control on two full passes, verdict lists identical), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits on both passes, production blobs byte-identical. No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text. Suite: 89 subtests green, 87.5% statement coverage; `GOOS=windows` builds.\\n- AC: 54 of 54 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`); crash/idempotency evidence via real SIGKILL between mkdir and fsync plus spawn-then-retry convergence. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n- BOUNDS: no real-tmux witness for any row (determinism design); Windows ownership is the creating-user ACL (tripwire-pinned); attach presentation vectors and lifecycle operations are sibling-leaf scope; registry bindings and the digest re-pin belong to the final leaf.\\n\\n## 2026-09-18\\n\\n### TASK-260830-32ypr2 — projection fidelity over captured bytes (FINAL leaf, STORY-260830-1cyj0q)\\n\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/cloneproject` implements the Section 13.14.1 projection-fidelity closure — `Normalize` derives a Canonical Session + Canonical Events from a sealed Clone Capture Manifest, its sealed Clone Raw Object Manifest, and blob bytes fetched through the real store layout. Unknown native types and unknown-class members become raw-addressable `opaque_event` records (`unknown_native_event`, ranges resolve to exact bytes); foreign encrypted/signed reasoning becomes byte-exact `opaque_reasoning` (`foreign_encrypted_payload`/`foreign_signature_unverifiable`, no content members); foreign instructions pin `low` authority and never reach the effective snapshot; tool calls resolve `completed` only with their result, else `aborted` history (`unsafe_pending_action`) with an always-empty live surface (pending needs a live work order, which capture never carries); source usage counts source-only; text over 64 KiB becomes an installed overflow blob reference (65536 inline / 65537 referenced, byte-exact). Every proof runs the real `clonesnap.Capture` entry first; every sealed byte re-decodes before return.\\n- EVIDENCE: package suite green (25 tests incl. the 33-row refusal table plus unstable/drift entries, determinism, idempotent replay, no-partial-bundle failure; 88.9% statement coverage); 49 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED, battery run twice with per-plant raw logs (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`), including two token-preserving rows killed by the behavioral suite and one verified cross-kill (the encrypted-gate plant also reddens the protected-message test). No `ax` command/doctor/capability claim; clause map + per-kind fact registry in `internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n- STORY-CLOSE: registry `section:7.8` and `section:10.2` unevidenced→full (2/2 + 5/5, excerpts re-measured, pin re-derived `69d156d9…2235052a` via the gate, shown in results); new acceptance cases `clone-capture-contracts`, `clone-native-capture`, `clone-projection-fidelity`, `session-adapter-call-binding`; `tracecheck` green at cases=144, full=4, partial=8, sliver=5, unevidenced=47, clauses 63/569 with `--section 7.8` and `--section 10.2` admitted; `section:13.14.1` deliberately unbound (scanner sees no RFC 2119 line — closed-shape sentences only — so a binding would measure `unmeasured` and fail assigned scope; record lives in the three TRACEABILITY files + matrices). Pin tests updated (report wants, sliver tables, 10.2 rename row now attacks `Capture`, admits lists extended to 7.8/10.2, README figure pins with `twelve`/`forty-seven`); README package section + measured-coverage rewrite (fenced line byte-equal).\\n- REFRESH: this run opened on stale base `a12d1bd` (branch tip `47294bb`) while trunk was `c3aae73`, so `refresh-candidate` ran FIRST (`refresh_advanced` onto `c3aae73`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay keeping trunk's 4qojoz entry newest-first). The audit restored trunk bytes for every carried stale revert (`.task-board`, `internal/meshneg`, `internal/rpcwire` tests/harness, `internal/matjournal` test, `task-board.config.json` back to the 30-command form); README/LOGBOOK/traceability edits were re-applied purely additively on the new bytes and the ownership registry MERGED (trunk's 5 cases + 3 upgraded bindings kept, this story's 4 cases + 2 bindings appended/transplanted — never replaced). Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 7 bounded groups incl. sessquery alone, 41/41 packages, no DATA RACE).\\n- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): fixture-native record envelope is test-defined framing (body shapes exact, envelope extras unclaimed); fact registries only for emitted kinds; native-protected records carry no reason code; turn IDs/source times null; call arguments not carried; SYNTHESIZED/partial/unavailable statuses and non-text content blocks never emitted (shape rules owned by the accepted clonebundle suite); 13.14.2–13.14.5 (fidelity dispositions, planning, lineage, transaction, tuple admission) sibling-owned; 7.8 operation frames stay `sessadapter`. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n- AC: 24 of 24 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests and measured with narrowings (matrix in `TASK-260830-32ypr2_conformance-matrix.md`).\\n- REV2 (rework of review RUN-260918-320878, CHANGES