w now attacks `Capture`, admits lists extended to 7.8/10.2, README figure pins with `twelve`/`forty-seven`); README package section + measured-coverage rewrite (fenced line byte-equal).\\n- REFRESH: this run opened on stale base `a12d1bd` (branch tip `47294bb`) while trunk was `c3aae73`, so `refresh-candidate` ran FIRST (`refresh_advanced` onto `c3aae73`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay keeping trunk's 4qojoz entry newest-first). The audit restored trunk bytes for every carried stale revert (`.task-board`, `internal/meshneg`, `internal/rpcwire` tests/harness, `internal/matjournal` test, `task-board.config.json` back to the 30-command form); README/LOGBOOK/traceability edits were re-applied purely additively on the new bytes and the ownership registry MERGED (trunk's 5 cases + 3 upgraded bindings kept, this story's 4 cases + 2 bindings appended/transplanted — never replaced). Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 7 bounded groups incl. sessquery alone, 41/41 packages, no DATA RACE).\\n- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): fixture-native record envelope is test-defined framing (body shapes exact, envelope extras unclaimed); fact registries only for emitted kinds; native-protected records carry no reason code; turn IDs/source times null; call arguments not carried; SYNTHESIZED/partial/unavailable statuses and non-text content blocks never emitted (shape rules owned by the accepted clonebundle suite); 13.14.2–13.14.5 (fidelity dispositions, planning, lineage, transaction, tuple admission) sibling-owned; 7.8 operation frames stay `sessadapter`. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n- AC: 24 of 24 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests and measured with narrowings (matrix in `TASK-260830-32ypr2_conformance-matrix.md`).\\n- REV2 (rework of review RUN-260918-320878, CHANGES REQUESTED; no base move, still `3005d78` over trunk `c3aae73`): P1-a CLOSED — envelope+body frame decodes delegate to `environ.DecodeStrictObject` at `strictMem