{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c9cb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c3b6-e69d-7952-b5c2-99ff4034d208"},"sequence":832,"recorded_at":1780531400001659,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5d75c7b3-ca89-4158-8f1c-936a31a9dfe8","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5d75c7b3-ca89-4158-8f1c-936a31a9dfe8","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5d75c7b3-ca89-4158-8f1c-936a31a9dfe8"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c3bb-2f79-7750-94c4-5e6a1372674b"},"task_id":"01a0c3bb-2f79-7750-94c4-5e6a1372674b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c3bb-2f79-7750-94c4-5e6a1372674b","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-17-1\",\n  \"command\": \"python3 -c \\\"\\nimport json\\ncfg=json.load(open('task-board.config.json'))\\ncmds=cfg['spawn']['worktree_isolation']['validation']['commands']\\nprint('count:',len(cmds))\\nfor i,c in enumerate(cmds,1):\\n    print(i,'|',c[:150])\\n\\\" 2>&1 | head -n 45\\necho \\\"=====README section=====\\\"\\nsed -n '2329,2385p' README.md\",\n  \"description\": \"List validation commands and README section\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"count: 30\\n1 | test -z \\\"$(gofmt -l $(git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard -- '*.go'))\\\"\\n2 | go build ./...\\n3 | go vet ./...\\n4 | go test ./... -count=1 -v\\n5 | go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m\\n6 | go test ./... -cover -count=1\\n7 | go test ./internal/rpcwire -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzUntrustedEnvelopes$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n8 | go test ./internal/rpcwire -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzClosedOperationBodies$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n9 | go test ./internal/rpcwire -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzNamespaceVocabulary$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n10 | go test ./internal/rpcwire -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzUnknownFields$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n11 | go test ./internal/scalar -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzScalarProductionEntries$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n12 | go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzCanonicalizeRoundTrip$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n13 | go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzObjectIdentityRepresentationInvariant$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n14 | go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzClosedIdentityShapeRefusal$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n15 | go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzObservationEventRefusal$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n16 | go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzCheckArgv$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n17 | go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzCheckMemberPath$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n18 | go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzIsEnvName$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n19 | go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzRedactCorpus$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n20 | go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzEscapeForTerminal$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n21 | go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzRenderForTerminal$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n22 | go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzGuardResolve$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n23 | go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzDetectCaseCollision$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n24 | go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\\n25 | go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\\n26 | GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...\\n27 | GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...\\n28 | git ls-files -z '*.json' | xargs -0 -n1 python3 -c 'import json,sys;json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))'\\n29 | task-board validate\\n30 | git diff --check\\n=====README section=====\\n## Private tmux server management (`tmuxserver` leaf)\\n\\n[`internal/tmuxserver`](internal/tmuxserver) creates owner-only runtime\\ndirectories and manages dedicated `tmux -S` servers with no ambient or\\ndefault-server discovery or reuse (pinned Sections 4.2, 4.C-4.E).\\n`EnsureRuntimeDir` commits the runtime leaf relative to a pinned root\\nhandle (`mkdirat`, never a path-string `MkdirAll`) and enforces three\\nindependent custody gates — containment, exact `0700` mode, effective-UID\\nownership — each of which refuses alone; an existing directory is\\nverified, never silently repaired. `ResolveSocket` derives the one\\nserver socket from the runtime directory and refuses any explicit\\noverride, whether it arrives as a `TMUX` environment value, an inherited\\nsocket, a default path, or the conventional `default` name. `Acquire`\\nreaches the server through the caller-appropriate path: foreground\\nattaches to the running attested server or spawns the dedicated `-S`\\nserver whose stable pane entrypoint is `ax pane SESSION_ID`, while\\nbackground contacts only the already-running authenticated broker and\\nits attested server, and otherwise returns the typed\\n`capability_unavailable` refusal with realm/readiness details — there is\\nno fallback to direct creation, and every background test arms a spy\\nspawner that fails the run if it is ever invoked. `CheckLiveAttestation`\\nadmits only a complete live observation (passed sentinel and\\nprovider-auth smoke bound to the exact server generation, provider\\nbuild, and macOS version); the `launchctl managername` hint and any\\ncached sentinel observation travel for diagnostics only and authorize\\nnothing. Every broker, server, and spawner interaction runs through\\ninjected dependencies, so the suite passes with no tmux process\\nanywhere.\\n\\nRun the focused tests and coverage with:\\n\\n```bash\\ngo test ./internal/tmuxserver -count=1\\ngo test ./internal/tmuxserver -cover -count=1\\n```\\n\\nRun the narrowing battery (29 narrowing mutants, one supplementary\\nadditive row, plus one harmless control) with:\\n\\n```bash\\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py\\n```\\n\\nThe harness mutates one production file in place, runs the named killer\\nthrough the production entry point, restores the file from backup, and\\nreports per-row verdicts with subprocess exits; `AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1`\\nadditionally prints the raw per-plant logs, and `--log-dir` captures one\\nraw log per plant. Task validation logs and mutation artifacts are\\nattached to `TASK-260830-35urbp`. The package adds no `ax` command, no\\n`doctor` result, and no runtime capability claim; the clause-to-test\\nmatrix with its stated bounds lives in\\n[the task evidence map](internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md).\\n\\n## Ownership reducer properties\\n\\nThe four story-pinned ownership invariants (pinned v0.6.0 Sections 2.2, 5.3,\\nand 13.6-13.10) hold as executable property tests over the landed production\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5284,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1321,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
