nt-mismatch: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly directory handles past the handle-binding check; the mismatch still refuses for non-directories. [exit 1]\\nok: N-containment-symlink: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly symlink leaves via an ELOOP fallback open; every other commit failure still refuses. [exit 1]\\nok: N-containment-symlink-verify: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly symlink leaves via an ELOOP fallback open on the verify side; the commit side still refuses. Kill path: Verify follows the leaf and the mode gate passes on the target. [exit 1]\\nok: N-root-wiring: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the relative-root fixture past our wiring of the landed grammar; every other malformed root still refuses. Kill reroutes to the guard refusal. [exit 1]\\nok: N-platform-wiring: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the plan9 platform past our wiring of the landed vocabulary; every other unknown platform still refuses. Kill reroutes to the root refusal. [exit 1]\\nok: N-platform-windows: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the C: fixture root past the lexical Windows refusal; every other Windows root still refuses there. Kill reroutes to the host arm, which reports runtime platform host instead of runtime platform. [exit 1]\\nok: N-override-env: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the TMUX environment value as an override; the other four vectors still refuse. [exit 1]\\nok: N-override-inherited: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the inherited socket as an override; the other four vectors still refuse. [exit 1]\\nok: N-override-default: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the default path as an override; the other four vectors still refuse. [exit 1]\\nok: N-override-conventional: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the conventional name as an override; the other four vectors still refuse. [exit 1]\\nok: N-override-tmpdir: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the TMUX_TMPDIR value as an override — the member tmux uses to relocate