{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d2cb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c3b6-e69d-7952-b5c2-99ff4034d208"},"sequence":1984,"recorded_at":1780531400003963,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5d75c7b3-ca89-4158-8f1c-936a31a9dfe8","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"5d75c7b3-ca89-4158-8f1c-936a31a9dfe8","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5d75c7b3-ca89-4158-8f1c-936a31a9dfe8"},"call_id":"call_01a0c3c80a9d7206805aa392a3bf1285","text":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 2336-2366\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-independent custody gates — containment, exact `0700` mode, effective-UID\n-ownership — each of which refuses alone; an existing directory is\n-verified, never silently repaired. `ResolveSocket` derives the one\n-server socket from the runtime directory and refuses any explicit\n-override, whether it arrives as a `TMUX` environment value, an inherited\n-socket, a default path, or the conventional `default` name. `Acquire`\n-reaches the server through the caller-appropriate path: foreground\n-attaches to the running attested server or spawns the dedicated `-S`\n-server whose stable pane entrypoint is `ax pane SESSION_ID`, while\n-background contacts only the already-running authenticated broker and\n-its attested server, and otherwise returns the typed\n-`capability_unavailable` refusal with realm/readiness details — there is\n-no fallback to direct creation, and every background test arms a spy\n-spawner that fails the run if it is ever invoked. `CheckLiveAttestation`\n-admits only a complete live observation (passed sentinel and\n-provider-auth smoke bound to the exact server generation, provider\n-build, and macOS version); the `launchctl managername` hint and any\n-cached sentinel observation travel for diagnostics only and authorize\n-nothing. Every broker, server, and spawner interaction runs through\n-injected dependencies, so the suite passes with no tmux process\n-anywhere.\n-\n-Run the focused tests and coverage with:\n-\n-```bash\n-go test ./internal/tmuxserver -count=1\n-go test ./internal/tmuxserver -cover -count=1\n-```\n-\n-Run the narrowing battery (29 narrowing mutants, one supplementary\n-additive row, plus one harmless control) with:\n+independent custody gates — containment, exact `0700` mode, effective-UID\n+ownership — each of which refuses alone; an existing directory is\n+verified, never silently repaired. `ResolveSocket` derives the one\n+server socket from the runtime directory and refuses any explicit\n+override on all five ambient members (`TMUX` and `TMUX_TMPDIR`\n+environment values, inherited socket, default path, conventional\n+`default` name). `Acquire` reaches the server through the\n+caller-appropriate path: foreground ensures the directory, then attaches\n+to the running attested server or spawns the dedicated `-S` server whose\n+stable pane entrypoint is `ax pane SESSION_ID`, while background\n+verifies the existing directory without creating it, contacts only the\n+already-running authenticated same-user broker and its attested server,\n+and otherwise returns the typed `capability_unavailable` refusal with\n+realm/readiness details — there is no fallback to direct creation, and\n+every background test arms a spy spawner that fails the run if it is\n+ever invoked. Attestation is the landed `terminalbackend`\n+Reconcile/ResolveEvidence admission consumed as an `Admitted` set\n+composed only with generation equality: a missing realm row or a\n+stale-generation admission refuses, so a cached observation replayed as\n+live authorizes nothing. Every broker, server, and spawner interaction\n+runs through injected dependencies, so the suite passes with no tmux\n+process anywhere; native Windows refuses every request.\n+\n+Run the focused tests and coverage with:\n+\n+```bash\n+go test ./internal/tmuxserver -count=1\n+go test ./internal/tmuxserver -cover -count=1\n+```\n+\n+Run the narrowing battery (40 narrowing mutants, one supplementary\n+additive row, plus one harmless control) with:\n","edit_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","path":"README.md","added":32,"removed":31},"correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","outcome":"success"}}}
